@startuml 15-payment-statuses
!include _style.iuml
title Payment statuses

[*] --> CREATED : order created at the provider\n(an open order is reused)
CREATED --> SUCCEEDED : confirmed by verify,\nwebhook or reconcile
CREATED --> FAILED : payment failed event
FAILED --> SUCCEEDED : later attempt on the\nsame order succeeds
FAILED --> FAILED : amount mismatch\n(reviewReason set)
SUCCEEDED --> REFUND_PENDING : booking cancelled with refund,\npaid twice, or booking could not be kept
REFUND_PENDING --> REFUNDED : provider accepted the refund
REFUND_PENDING --> REFUND_PENDING : attempt failed,\nretry after back-off
REFUND_PENDING --> REFUND_FAILED : 5 attempts failed
REFUND_FAILED --> REFUND_PENDING : admin presses retry
REFUNDED --> [*]

note right of REFUND_FAILED
  Shown in the admin list
  "payments needing attention".
end note
note left of SUCCEEDED
  Once SUCCEEDED or in a refund state,
  late payment events are ignored.
  A guest cancel inside the no-refund
  window leaves it SUCCEEDED.
end note
@enduml
